# Environments
.env
venv/
venv-docling/
env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Credentials. Broad on purpose: this project has committed an OAuth client
# secret to a shared branch before, and a pattern costs nothing to keep.
credentials.json
client_secret.json
token.json
*.pem
*.key

# OS / Editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Logs
logs/*.log

# Input corpus and all regenerated pipeline output. The numbered sustainability
# folders contain the transferred Docling cache and fused-page cache.
data/01_raw/
data/02_interim/
data/03_sections/sustainability/
data/04_chunks/
data/05_db/
data/05_embedding/
data/00_reference/*
!data/00_reference/.gitkeep
!data/00_reference/companies.csv
!data/00_reference/sustainability_report_tracker.csv
outputs/**

# Handoff packages and their archives. These are rebuilt from a chunk index by
# esg/scripts/build_chunk_handoff.py, so the script is the thing worth keeping;
# a single full-corpus handout is roughly 400 MB and must never reach history.
data/handout*/
data/handoff*/
data/_pre_run_backups/
data/*.db
data/*.tar
data/*.zip
# SQLite sidecars. A build in progress leaves esg.db-journal behind, and the
# transfer guide fails the package outright if a live WAL, SHM or journal file
# reaches the archive -- it means the database was copied while a writer was
# still attached and is not a consistent snapshot.
data/*.db-journal
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm

# Disposable local work. Keep only the cleanup rules readable in Git.
scratchpad/**
!scratchpad/
!scratchpad/README.md

# QA snapshots are regenerated per run and stamped with the database hash.
reports/**
!reports/

# Local backup snapshots and scratch, never for history.
data/_pre_promotion_backups/
.codex_tmp/

# Inputs, not regenerated outputs: the fusion bridge reads these for source
# identity and cannot mint the IDs itself, so a clean clone must carry them.
!data/00_reference/esg_parse_index.csv
!data/00_reference/esg_accepted_company_manifest.csv
# Same rule, learned the hard way: without the catalog the QA database loads
# every document, section and chunk against five empty identity tables and
# comes out with 140,027 foreign key violations, silently -- the build reports
# success. The approvals file is empty today but is the same class of input.
!data/00_reference/esg_file_catalog.csv
!data/00_reference/esg_ocr_approval.csv
# The Drive snapshot. Previously left out as a disposable local artifact, but
# it is the only evidence tying the corpus to its source: the 2026-08-12 copy
# is what proved all 681 PDFs match Drive byte for byte. A clean clone with no
# Drive access cannot regenerate it, and the stale copy it replaced had wrong
# hashes for two files -- which is exactly the sort of thing a committed,
# dated snapshot makes reviewable.
!data/00_reference/esg_drive_manifest.csv
